<%# The playing record's cover fills the whole floor — no margins — blown up,
    blurred and dimmed so the glass above it reads. Two layers cross-fade on
    every change, and it rides Turbo's permanent flag so a visit doesn't reset
    the wash. The player controller paints it. The blur/dim live inline: their
    arbitrary Tailwind forms don't survive the build. %>
<div id="backdrop" data-turbo-permanent aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 overflow-hidden">
  <div data-player-target="backdrop"
       class="absolute inset-0 bg-cover bg-center opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-[1200ms] ease-out"
       style="transform: scale(1.25); filter: blur(56px) saturate(1.6) brightness(0.5);"></div>
  <div data-player-target="backdrop"
       class="absolute inset-0 bg-cover bg-center opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-[1200ms] ease-out"
       style="transform: scale(1.25); filter: blur(56px) saturate(1.6) brightness(0.5);"></div>
</div>
